rete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "First vs. Zero Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Zero Conditional</span> is used to talk about things that are always true. These can be facts, or  things you generally do in a given situation. <br>You use the<span class=\"strong\"> First Conditional</span> with <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clauses when you consider what you might possibly do in the future under a certain condition.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The<span class=\"strong\"> Zero Conditional</span>, also called the Present Real Conditional uses the following structure: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If/when</span></span>  \u2026 Simple Present, \u2026 Simple Present <br>or<br> Simple Present \u2026 <span class=\"strong\">if/when</span> \u2026 Simple Present.</span> <br> <br>Both <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> if</span> and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> are used in the Present Real Conditional. Using<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> if</span> </span> suggests that something happens less frequently. Using <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> when</span></span>  suggests that it is fairly certain the condition will be fulfilled. <br> <br>You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will, or will not happen. The outcome is not in the present, but in the future. <br> <br>Structure: <br><span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple \u2026 will + verb \u2026</span><br>or<br> <span class=\"italic\">will + verb .... + if + Present Simple</span><br> <br> If people overeat, they become overweight. <br> If it rains on Saturday, I will stay home and watch a movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">When</span> people feel threatened they act out.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">When</span> you take a breath, your heart opens and you listen without judgement. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">When</span> you order something and the restaurant runs out of it, it's frustrating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> you want to provide the best service, you start by finding out what customers want.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Purpose and Intention", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Besides using linking clauses to express your purpose, you can use certain nouns or verbal phrases to state your intentions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to express purpose and intention, the following phrases and expressions can be used. <br> <br> <ul><li>Nouns/Verbal phrases <br><span class=\"italic\">To have +<span class=\"strong\">  high hopes of</span> /<span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"strong\">no intention of </span>/<span class=\"strong\"> no thoughts of </span>/<span class=\"strong\"> half a mind to ...</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">To be + / <span class=\"strong\">toying with the idea</span> ...</span></li><li>Prepositional phrases<br><span class=\"italic\">+<span class=\"strong\">  in the hopes of getting</span> / +<span class=\"strong\">  with a view to getting </span>/ +<span class=\"strong\">  with the aim of getting </span>...</span> </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I have no real intention of saying anything.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I think that the customer complained with the aim of hurting someone. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I have half a mind to call him out.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to act out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to behave in an angry way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When people feel threatened they act out.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about dealing wih customers.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "outright", "type": "name"}, {"content": "obviously ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When someone lies outright like that, it gets my back up.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get one's back up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make someone angry;  become upset ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When someone lies outright like that, it gets my back up.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "for the sake of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "out of consideration for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For the sake of your own well-being, I think you will have to keep a lid on it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep a lid on it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be quiet about something or to keep a situation under control", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For the sake of your own well-being, I think you will have to keep a lid on it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have one's heart set on something", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to want something badly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When someone has their heart set on something, they cannot be stopped! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be held accountable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be responsible for ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can't be held accountable for someone else's mental health issues in the workplace.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "repeat business ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "regular business from the same customers ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You've also had a lot of repeat business. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Find 2 partners to have a group of 3.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You and your friend are at a restaurant and the waiter (your partner) brought you the wrong order, spilled soda on you and you found a hair in your soup. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss with your friend whether or not to tell the manager about it.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about customer relations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express my intentions in dealing with customers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I speak about possibilities.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}